/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 2 Kings chapters 21-25
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("2kings", [
{n:21, name:"Manasseh and Amon", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 21:13",verse:"And I will stretch over Jerusalem the line of Samaria, and the plummet of the house of Ahab: and I will wipe Jerusalem as a man wipeth a dish, wiping it, and turning it upside down."}, facts:["Did you know Manasseh reigned fifty-five years, the longest reign of any king of Judah or Israel (2 Kings 21:1)?","Did you know God measured doomed Jerusalem with 'the line of Samaria, and the plummet of the house of Ahab,' a builder's tools turned to judgment (2 Kings 21:13)?","Did you know Amon's own servants murdered him in his house, and the people of the land slew the conspirators and crowned his eight-year-old son Josiah (2 Kings 21:23-24)?"], questions:[
{q:"How old was Manasseh when he began to reign, and how long did he reign?", options:["Twelve, and he reigned fifty and five years","Eight, and he reigned thirty and one years","Twenty-two, and he reigned two years","Twenty-five, and he reigned eleven years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:1",verse:"Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and reigned fifty and five years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Hephzi-bah.", insight:"Twelve years old and fifty-five years of power; a long reign is measured by what it served, not by how long it lasted."},
{q:"What was the name of Manasseh's mother?", options:["Hephzibah","Meshullemeth","Jedidah","Hamutal"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:1",verse:"Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and reigned fifty and five years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Hephzi-bah.", insight:"Hephzibah means 'my delight is in her'; a mother's delight cannot guarantee a son's devotion."},
{q:"After whose abominations did Manasseh do evil?", options:["The heathen, whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel","The kings of Assyria","The priests of Egypt","The prophets of Baal alone"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:2",verse:"And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, after the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel.", insight:"Evil in the sight of the LORD is the only verdict that matters; men's applause never overrules it."},
{q:"What did Manasseh build up again, which Hezekiah his father had destroyed?", options:["The high places","The walls of Jerusalem","The temple courts","The royal palace"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:3",verse:"For he built up again the high places which Hezekiah his father had destroyed; and he reared up altars for Baal, and made a grove, as did Ahab king of Israel; and worshipped all the host of heaven, and served them.", insight:"He rebuilt what his father tore down; every generation must choose which father's work it continues."},
{q:"Which king of Israel had done the same in making a grove?", options:["Ahab","Jeroboam","Omri","Jehu"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:3",verse:"For he built up again the high places which Hezekiah his father had destroyed; and he reared up altars for Baal, and made a grove, as did Ahab king of Israel; and worshipped all the host of heaven, and served them.", insight:"He copied Ahab, the worst of Israel's kings; imitate the godly, not the merely powerful."},
{q:"Where did Manasseh set altars for all the host of heaven?", options:["In the two courts of the house of the LORD","On the Mount of Olives","In the valley of Hinnom","At the gates of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:5",verse:"And he built altars for all the host of heaven in the two courts of the house of the LORD.", insight:"Altars to the stars in the very courts of God's house; compromise moves one step at a time into the sanctuary."},
{q:"What did Manasseh do to his own son?", options:["He made him pass through the fire","He made him a priest of Baal","He sent him to Assyria","He crowned him king"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:6",verse:"And he made his son pass through the fire, and observed times, and used enchantments, and dealt with familiar spirits and wizards: he wrought much wickedness in the sight of the LORD, to provoke him to anger.", insight:"He made his son pass through the fire; idolatry always demands what you love most."},
{q:"Which forbidden practices are named in his reign?", options:["Observing times, enchantments, familiar spirits, and wizards","Offering peace offerings and tithes","Building synagogues and schools","Keeping feasts and fasts"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:6",verse:"And he made his son pass through the fire, and observed times, and used enchantments, and dealt with familiar spirits and wizards: he wrought much wickedness in the sight of the LORD, to provoke him to anger.", insight:"Times, enchantments, spirits, wizards: when men reject God's word, they will listen to anything else."},
{q:"What had the LORD said about the house where Manasseh set his graven image?", options:["In this house, and in Jerusalem, will I put my name for ever","It would stand until the end of the world","The nations would worship there","Its stones would never fall"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:7",verse:"And he set a graven image of the grove that he had made in the house, of which the LORD said to David, and to Solomon his son, In this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all tribes of Israel, will I put my name for ever:", insight:"God put His name in that house forever; sacred places carry promises that outlast their polluters."},
{q:"What was promised if Israel would observe all the LORD commanded?", options:["Their feet would move no more out of the land","They would rule all nations","Their enemies would serve them","Their gold would never fail"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:8",verse:"Neither will I make the feet of Israel move any more out of the land which I gave their fathers; only if they will observe to do according to all that I have commanded them, and according to all the law that my servant Moses commanded them.", insight:"God's promise was tied to obedience; covenant blessing follows covenant faithfulness."},
{q:"How did Manasseh's evil compare with the nations?", options:["He seduced Judah to do more evil than the nations the LORD destroyed","It was milder than theirs","It matched theirs exactly","It was hidden and secret"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:9",verse:"But they hearkened not: and Manasseh seduced them to do more evil than did the nations whom the LORD destroyed before the children of Israel.", insight:"Manasseh outdid the nations God had destroyed; leadership can make a whole people worse than their enemies."},
{q:"By whom did the LORD speak His warning against Manasseh?", options:["By His servants the prophets","By the priests of the temple","By dreams to the king","By the elders of Judah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:10",verse:"And the LORD spake by his servants the prophets, saying,", insight:"The LORD spoke by His servants the prophets; God always warns before He wounds."},
{q:"What would happen to whoever heard of the coming evil?", options:["Both his ears shall tingle","He would flee to Egypt","He would be struck blind","He would lose his inheritance"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:12",verse:"Therefore thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Behold, I am bringing such evil upon Jerusalem and Judah, that whosoever heareth of it, both his ears shall tingle.", insight:"Both ears shall tingle; judgment this shocking deserves a hearing."},
{q:"What image does God use for what He would do to Jerusalem?", options:["Wipe it as a man wipeth a dish, wiping it, and turning it upside down","Scatter it as chaff before the wind","Melt it as wax before fire","Plow it as a field"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:13",verse:"And I will stretch over Jerusalem the line of Samaria, and the plummet of the house of Ahab: and I will wipe Jerusalem as a man wipeth a dish, wiping it, and turning it upside down.", insight:"Jerusalem wiped like a dish and turned upside down; God can cleanse the vessel or discard it."},
{q:"How much innocent blood did Manasseh shed?", options:["Till he had filled Jerusalem from one end to another","Only in the temple courts","A small amount, quickly repented","None, for he feared the law"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:16",verse:"Moreover Manasseh shed innocent blood very much, till he had filled Jerusalem from one end to another; beside his sin wherewith he made Judah to sin, in doing that which was evil in the sight of the LORD.", insight:"He filled Jerusalem with innocent blood from end to end; cruelty has a ledger, and God keeps the books."},
{q:"Where was Manasseh buried?", options:["In the garden of his own house, in the garden of Uzza","In the sepulchres of the kings","In the valley of Hinnom","In the city of David"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:18",verse:"And Manasseh slept with his fathers, and was buried in the garden of his own house, in the garden of Uzza: and Amon his son reigned in his stead.", insight:"Buried in his own garden; the wicked king's splendor shrank to a private plot of earth."},
{q:"How old was Amon when he began to reign, and how long did he reign?", options:["Twenty-two, and he reigned two years","Twelve, and he reigned fifty-five years","Eight, and he reigned thirty-one years","Twenty-three, and he reigned three months"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:19",verse:"Amon was twenty and two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned two years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Meshullemeth, the daughter of Haruz of Jotbah.", insight:"Twenty-two, reigning two years; a short reign can still be an entirely evil one."},
{q:"What was the name of Amon's mother?", options:["Meshullemeth, the daughter of Haruz of Jotbah","Hephzibah of Jerusalem","Jedidah of Boscath","Zebudah of Rumah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:19",verse:"Amon was twenty and two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned two years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Meshullemeth, the daughter of Haruz of Jotbah.", insight:"Meshullemeth of Jotbah; Scripture remembers mothers even when kings forget God."},
{q:"How did Amon die?", options:["His servants conspired against him, and slew him in his own house","He fell in battle with Assyria","He died of a plague in Jerusalem","He was carried captive to Babylon"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:23",verse:"And the servants of Amon conspired against him, and slew the king in his own house.", insight:"Slain by his own servants in his own house; those who rule by evil are rarely safe from it."},
{q:"Whom did the people of the land make king after slaying the conspirators?", options:["Josiah his son","Jehoahaz his brother","A captain of the guard","A priest of the temple"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 21:24",verse:"And the people of the land slew all them that had conspired against king Amon; and the people of the land made Josiah his son king in his stead.", insight:"The people crowned Josiah, an eight-year-old; God can raise a reformer from the ruins of two bad reigns."}
]},
{n:22, name:"The Book Found", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 22:19",verse:"Because thine heart was tender, and thou hast humbled thyself before the LORD, when thou heardest what I spake against this place, and against the inhabitants thereof, that they should become a desolation and a curse, and hast rent thy clothes, and wept before me; I also have heard thee, saith the LORD."}, facts:["Did you know the Book of the Law found in the temple was likely Deuteronomy, whose covenant curses matched exactly what Huldah confirmed (2 Kings 22:8)?","Did you know the king's delegation sought out a woman? Huldah the prophetess, wife of Shallum the keeper of the wardrobe, spoke one of Scripture's plainest words of judgment (2 Kings 22:14).","Did you know the temple repair workers were never audited? 'There was no reckoning made with them of the money... because they dealt faithfully' (2 Kings 22:7)."], questions:[
{q:"How old was Josiah when he began to reign, and how long did he reign?", options:["Eight, and he reigned thirty and one years","Twelve, and he reigned fifty and five years","Twenty-one, and he reigned eleven years","Eighteen, and he reigned three months"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:1",verse:"Josiah was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned thirty and one years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jedidah, the daughter of Adaiah of Boscath.", insight:"Eight years old, thirty-one years on the throne; God can steady a kingdom through a child who will not turn aside."},
{q:"What was the name of Josiah's mother?", options:["Jedidah, the daughter of Adaiah of Boscath","Hephzibah of Jerusalem","Meshullemeth of Jotbah","Hamutal of Libnah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:1",verse:"Josiah was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned thirty and one years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jedidah, the daughter of Adaiah of Boscath.", insight:"Jedidah of Boscath; even in Manasseh's dark line, God preserved a mother who would raise a reformer."},
{q:"How is Josiah's reign described?", options:["He did right, walked in the way of David, and turned not aside to the right hand or to the left","He did evil as his father Manasseh did","He reigned well but kept the high places","He began well but turned away at the end"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:2",verse:"And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, and walked in all the way of David his father, and turned not aside to the right hand or to the left.", insight:"He turned not to the right hand or to the left; steadiness, not spectacle, marks the righteous king."},
{q:"In the eighteenth year of his reign, whom did Josiah send to the house of the LORD?", options:["Shaphan the scribe","Hilkiah the high priest","Ahikam the son of Shaphan","Asahiah the king's servant"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:3",verse:"And it came to pass in the eighteenth year of king Josiah, that the king sent Shaphan the son of Azaliah, the son of Meshullam, the scribe, to the house of the LORD, saying,", insight:"In his eighteenth year he sent Shaphan; godly kings attend to God's house, not only their own."},
{q:"What was Shaphan's lineage?", options:["The son of Azaliah, the son of Meshullam","The son of Hilkiah the priest","The son of Tikvah the scribe","The son of Harhas of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:3",verse:"And it came to pass in the eighteenth year of king Josiah, that the king sent Shaphan the son of Azaliah, the son of Meshullam, the scribe, to the house of the LORD, saying,", insight:"Shaphan son of Azaliah, son of Meshullam; faithful men are known by name and lineage in God's records."},
{q:"What was Hilkiah to sum up?", options:["The silver brought into the house of the LORD, gathered by the keepers of the door","The gold of the temple vessels","The tithes of the priests","The tribute owed to Assyria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:4",verse:"Go up to Hilkiah the high priest, that he may sum the silver which is brought into the house of the LORD, which the keepers of the door have gathered of the people:", insight:"Sum the silver the door keepers gathered; every offering of the people deserves honest counting."},
{q:"What was the silver to be used for?", options:["To repair the breaches of the house of the LORD","To pay tribute to the king of Egypt","To buy horses and chariots","To build a new palace"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:5",verse:"And let them deliver it into the hand of the doers of the work, that have the oversight of the house of the LORD: and let them give it to the doers of the work which is in the house of the LORD, to repair the breaches of the house,", insight:"Repair the breaches of the house; worship needs maintenance, and neglect shows in the walls."},
{q:"Which workmen were to receive the silver?", options:["Carpenters, builders, and masons","Goldsmiths and silversmiths","Scribes and Levites","Soldiers and watchmen"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:6",verse:"Unto carpenters, and builders, and masons, and to buy timber and hewn stone to repair the house.", insight:"Carpenters, builders, masons; God's work employs every craft, not only priests."},
{q:"Why was no reckoning made of the money given to the workmen?", options:["Because they dealt faithfully","Because the amount was small","Because the king trusted Hilkiah alone","Because the priests counted it daily"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:7",verse:"Howbeit there was no reckoning made with them of the money that was delivered into their hand, because they dealt faithfully.", insight:"No reckoning was made, because they dealt faithfully; integrity is the audit that never needs checking."},
{q:"What did Hilkiah the high priest find in the house of the LORD?", options:["The book of the law","A chest of gold","The ark of the covenant","A crown of David"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:8",verse:"And Hilkiah the high priest said unto Shaphan the scribe, I have found the book of the law in the house of the LORD. And Hilkiah gave the book to Shaphan, and he read it.", insight:"The book of the law, found in the house; the greatest treasure in the temple was not gold but God's word."},
{q:"What did Shaphan do with the book?", options:["He read it before the king","He hid it in the temple","He copied it for the priests","He sealed it in the treasury"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:10",verse:"And Shaphan the scribe shewed the king, saying, Hilkiah the priest hath delivered me a book. And Shaphan read it before the king.", insight:"Shaphan read it before the king; hearing God's word read aloud is where revival begins."},
{q:"What did Josiah do when he heard the words of the book?", options:["He rent his clothes","He called for his army","He shut the temple doors","He sent for the prophets"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:11",verse:"And it came to pass, when the king had heard the words of the book of the law, that he rent his clothes.", insight:"He rent his clothes; true hearing of God's word breaks the heart before it reforms the kingdom."},
{q:"Which five men did the king send to enquire of the LORD?", options:["Hilkiah, Ahikam, Achbor, Shaphan, and Asahiah","Nathan, Gad, Iddo, Shemaiah, and Azariah","Eliakim, Shebna, Joah, Hilkiah, and Shaphan","The elders of Judah and Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:12",verse:"And the king commanded Hilkiah the priest, and Ahikam the son of Shaphan, and Achbor the son of Michaiah, and Shaphan the scribe, and Asahiah a servant of the king’s, saying,", insight:"Five men sent to enquire; a humbled king seeks God's mind, not his own counsel."},
{q:"For whom were they to enquire of the LORD?", options:["For the king, and for the people, and for all Judah","For the army and the captains","For the priests and the Levites","For the king of Assyria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:13",verse:"Go ye, enquire of the LORD for me, and for the people, and for all Judah, concerning the words of this book that is found: for great is the wrath of the LORD that is kindled against us, because our fathers have not hearkened unto the words of this book, to do according unto all that which is written concerning us.", insight:"'Enquire for me, and for the people'; conviction should drive us to God, not to despair."},
{q:"Who was Huldah the prophetess?", options:["The wife of Shallum the keeper of the wardrobe","The daughter of Hilkiah the priest","The widow of a prophet of Samaria","The nurse of king Josiah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:14",verse:"So Hilkiah the priest, and Ahikam, and Achbor, and Shaphan, and Asahiah, went unto Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum the son of Tikvah, the son of Harhas, keeper of the wardrobe; (now she dwelt in Jerusalem in the college;) and they communed with her.", insight:"Huldah the prophetess, wife of the wardrobe keeper; God speaks through whom He chooses, and kings do well to listen."},
{q:"How did Huldah address the king who sent the delegation?", options:["Tell the man that sent you to me","Tell the righteous king","Tell the son of David","Tell the keeper of the covenant"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:15",verse:"And she said unto them, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Tell the man that sent you to me,", insight:"'Tell the man that sent you'; even kings are simply 'the man' before God's word."},
{q:"What did the LORD say He would bring upon Jerusalem?", options:["Evil upon this place, even all the words of the book the king had read","A new covenant of peace","Wealth and plenty for a generation","Victory over all their enemies"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:16",verse:"Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will bring evil upon this place, and upon the inhabitants thereof, even all the words of the book which the king of Judah hath read:", insight:"Evil on this place, even all the words of the book; God's warnings are as sure as His promises."},
{q:"Why would God's wrath be kindled and not quenched?", options:["Because they had forsaken Him and burned incense unto other gods","Because the temple was in ruins","Because the priests had fled","Because the book had been lost"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:17",verse:"Because they have forsaken me, and have burned incense unto other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the works of their hands; therefore my wrath shall be kindled against this place, and shall not be quenched.", insight:"Wrath kindled and not quenched; forsaking God is a fire men light but cannot put out."},
{q:"Why did the LORD say He had heard Josiah?", options:["Because his heart was tender, he humbled himself, rent his clothes, and wept before the LORD","Because he offered a thousand sacrifices","Because he rebuilt the temple walls","Because he defeated the Assyrians"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:19",verse:"Because thine heart was tender, and thou hast humbled thyself before the LORD, when thou heardest what I spake against this place, and against the inhabitants thereof, that they should become a desolation and a curse, and hast rent thy clothes, and wept before me; I also have heard thee, saith the LORD.", insight:"A tender heart, rent clothes, tears: these are the things God says He has heard."},
{q:"What mercy was promised to Josiah?", options:["He would be gathered to his grave in peace, and his eyes would not see the evil","He would live to see Jerusalem restored","His sons would reign forever","The captivity would never come"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 22:20",verse:"Behold therefore, I will gather thee unto thy fathers, and thou shalt be gathered into thy grave in peace; and thine eyes shall not see all the evil which I will bring upon this place. And they brought the king word again.", insight:"Gathered to his grave in peace; God sometimes shelters His servant from the storm He will not turn back."}
]},
{n:23, name:"Josiah's Reforms", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 23:25",verse:"And like unto him was there no king before him, that turned to the LORD with all his heart, and with all his soul, and with all his might, according to all the law of Moses; neither after him arose there any like him."}, facts:["Did you know Josiah's burning of bones on Jeroboam's altar at Bethel fulfilled a prophecy spoken about three hundred years earlier by the man of God from Judah (2 Kings 23:16-17)?","Did you know no Passover like this had been kept since the days of the judges, centuries before any king of Israel or Judah (2 Kings 23:22)?","Did you know the valley of Hinnom, where Topheth's fires passed children through to Molech, is Ge-Hinnom, the root of Gehenna, the New Testament word for hell (2 Kings 23:10)?"], questions:[
{q:"Whom did the king gather unto him at Jerusalem?", options:["All the elders of Judah and of Jerusalem","The captains of the army","The merchants of the city","The prophets of Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:1",verse:"And the king sent, and they gathered unto him all the elders of Judah and of Jerusalem.", insight:"He gathered all the elders, small and great; covenant renewal starts when leaders and people hear together."},
{q:"What did the king read in the ears of all the people?", options:["All the words of the book of the covenant","The chronicles of the kings","The song of Moses","The names of the tribes"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:2",verse:"And the king went up into the house of the LORD, and all the men of Judah and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem with him, and the priests, and the prophets, and all the people, both small and great: and he read in their ears all the words of the book of the covenant which was found in the house of the LORD.", insight:"He read in their ears all the words; the book must be read aloud, not shelved."},
{q:"Where did the king stand when he made the covenant?", options:["By a pillar","On the temple steps","At the brazen altar","In the king's gate"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:3",verse:"And the king stood by a pillar, and made a covenant before the LORD, to walk after the LORD, and to keep his commandments and his testimonies and his statutes with all their heart and all their soul, to perform the words of this covenant that were written in this book. And all the people stood to the covenant.", insight:"Standing by a pillar, he covenanted with all his heart and soul; public promises make private devotion accountable."},
{q:"What was done with the vessels made for Baal, the grove, and the host of heaven?", options:["They were burned without Jerusalem in the fields of Kidron","They were stored in the temple treasury","They were given to the priests","They were thrown into the sea"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:4",verse:"And the king commanded Hilkiah the high priest, and the priests of the second order, and the keepers of the door, to bring forth out of the temple of the LORD all the vessels that were made for Baal, and for the grove, and for all the host of heaven: and he burned them without Jerusalem in the fields of Kidron, and carried the ashes of them unto Bethel.", insight:"Vessels of Baal burned in the fields of Kidron; idolatry's tools deserve the fire, not the museum."},
{q:"Whom did Josiah put down?", options:["The idolatrous priests whom the kings of Judah had ordained","The Levites of the temple","The scribes of the law","The elders of the city"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:5",verse:"And he put down the idolatrous priests, whom the kings of Judah had ordained to burn incense in the high places in the cities of Judah, and in the places round about Jerusalem; them also that burned incense unto Baal, to the sun, and to the moon, and to the planets, and to all the host of heaven.", insight:"He put down the priests the kings had ordained; reform must remove the personnel of falsehood, not only its props."},
{q:"What did Josiah do to the grove in the house of the LORD?", options:["Brought it to the brook Kidron, burned it, stamped it to powder, and cast it on the graves","Buried it under the temple","Set it up in Bethel","Sold it to the merchants"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:6",verse:"And he brought out the grove from the house of the LORD, without Jerusalem, unto the brook Kidron, and burned it at the brook Kidron, and stamped it small to powder, and cast the powder thereof upon the graves of the children of the people.", insight:"The grove burned, stamped to powder, cast on graves; Josiah made idolatry as dishonorable as a cemetery."},
{q:"Whose houses did the king break down by the house of the LORD?", options:["The houses of the sodomites","The houses of the merchants","The houses of the gatekeepers","The houses of the singers"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:7",verse:"And he brake down the houses of the sodomites, that were by the house of the LORD, where the women wove hangings for the grove.", insight:"Houses of the sodomites by the house of the LORD; sin set up beside the sanctuary still has to come down."},
{q:"What did the women weave in those houses?", options:["Hangings for the grove","Garments for the priests","Curtains for the temple","Ropes for the sacrifices"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:7",verse:"And he brake down the houses of the sodomites, that were by the house of the LORD, where the women wove hangings for the grove.", insight:"Women wove hangings for the grove; falsehood always recruits busy hands to dress it up."},
{q:"Over what span did Josiah defile the high places?", options:["From Geba to Beer-sheba","From Dan to Bethel","From Jerusalem to Samaria","From Gilgal to Jericho"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:8",verse:"And he brought all the priests out of the cities of Judah, and defiled the high places where the priests had burned incense, from Geba to Beer-sheba, and brake down the high places of the gates that were in the entering in of the gate of Joshua the governor of the city, which were on a man’s left hand at the gate of the city.", insight:"From Geba to Beer-sheba the high places fell; half-hearted reform leaves the borders standing."},
{q:"What was Topheth, which Josiah defiled?", options:["In the valley of Hinnom, where children were passed through fire to Molech","A high place on the Mount of Olives","A grove in the king's garden","An altar in the temple court"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:10",verse:"And he defiled Topheth, which is in the valley of the children of Hinnom, that no man might make his son or his daughter to pass through the fire to Molech.", insight:"Topheth defiled, so no child would pass through fire to Molech; a king's zeal can stop even the cruelest rites."},
{q:"What did Josiah do with the horses given to the sun?", options:["He took them away, and burned the chariots of the sun with fire","He gave them to the priests","He sent them to Egypt","He set them free in the fields"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:11",verse:"And he took away the horses that the kings of Judah had given to the sun, at the entering in of the house of the LORD, by the chamber of Nathan-melech the chamberlain, which was in the suburbs, and burned the chariots of the sun with fire.", insight:"Horses and chariots dedicated to the sun went into the fire; no tribute may be paid to created things."},
{q:"Which altars did the king beat down and cast into the brook Kidron?", options:["The altars of Ahaz, and the altars Manasseh had made in the two courts","The altar of Solomon in Gibeon","The altars of the patriarchs","The altars of the northern tribes"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:12",verse:"And the altars that were on the top of the upper chamber of Ahaz, which the kings of Judah had made, and the altars which Manasseh had made in the two courts of the house of the LORD, did the king beat down, and brake them down from thence, and cast the dust of them into the brook Kidron.", insight:"Altars of Ahaz and of Manasseh beaten down; godly children may have to dismantle what ungodly fathers built."},
{q:"What did Josiah defile on the mount of corruption?", options:["The high places Solomon had built for Ashtoreth, Chemosh, and Milcom","The tombs of the ancient kings","The watchtowers of Jerusalem","The threshingfloors of the priests"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:13",verse:"And the high places that were before Jerusalem, which were on the right hand of the mount of corruption, which Solomon the king of Israel had builded for Ashtoreth the abomination of the Zidonians, and for Chemosh the abomination of the Moabites, and for Milcom the abomination of the children of Ammon, did the king defile.", insight:"Solomon's own high places on the mount of corruption defiled; old compromises by great men still count as sin."},
{q:"What did Josiah do after breaking the images and cutting down the groves?", options:["He filled their places with the bones of men","He planted vineyards there","He built watchtowers on them","He sowed them with salt"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:14",verse:"And he brake in pieces the images, and cut down the groves, and filled their places with the bones of men.", insight:"He filled the shrines' places with the bones of men; desecration was the fitting end of defilement."},
{q:"What did Josiah do to the altar at Bethel?", options:["He brake it down, burned the high place, and burned the grove","He repaired it for the priests","He covered it with gold","He moved it to Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:15",verse:"Moreover the altar that was at Bethel, and the high place which Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin, had made, both that altar and the high place he brake down, and burned the high place, and stamped it small to powder, and burned the grove.", insight:"Jeroboam's altar at Bethel broken and burned; no shrine, however historic, outranks God's word."},
{q:"Whose bones did Josiah refuse to move?", options:["The man of God who came from Judah, who had prophesied against the altar","The bones of Jeroboam the king","The bones of the priests of Samaria","The bones of the kings of Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:18",verse:"And he said, Let him alone; let no man move his bones. So they let his bones alone, with the bones of the prophet that came out of Samaria.", insight:"'Let him alone; let no man move his bones'; Josiah honored the prophet who had honored God."},
{q:"What did Josiah do to the priests of the high places in Samaria?", options:["He slew them upon the altars, and burned men's bones upon them","He carried them captive to Jerusalem","He made them priests of the temple","He set them to repair the walls"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:20",verse:"And he slew all the priests of the high places that were there upon the altars, and burned men’s bones upon them, and returned to Jerusalem.", insight:"He slew the priests of the high places on their own altars; false priests shared the fate of their false worship."},
{q:"How does Scripture describe Josiah's Passover?", options:["There was not holden such a passover from the days of the judges","It was the first passover ever kept","It lasted only one day","It was kept in Samaria, not Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:22",verse:"Surely there was not holden such a passover from the days of the judges that judged Israel, nor in all the days of the kings of Israel, nor of the kings of Judah;", insight:"No such passover since the days of the judges; when the word returns, the feast returns."},
{q:"How is Josiah summed up among the kings?", options:["Like unto him was there no king before him, that turned to the LORD with all his heart, soul, and might","He was the richest of all the kings","He reigned the longest of all","He built the greatest temple"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:25",verse:"And like unto him was there no king before him, that turned to the LORD with all his heart, and with all his soul, and with all his might, according to all the law of Moses; neither after him arose there any like him.", insight:"No king like him, turning with all heart, soul, and might; whole-heartedness is the highest praise a king can earn."},
{q:"How did Josiah die?", options:["Pharaoh-nechoh king of Egypt slew him at Megiddo","He was slain by his own servants","He died of old age in Jerusalem","He fell in battle with Babylon"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 23:29",verse:"In his days Pharaoh-nechoh king of Egypt went up against the king of Assyria to the river Euphrates: and king Josiah went against him; and he slew him at Megiddo, when he had seen him.", insight:"Slain at Megiddo by Pharaoh-nechoh; even a good king's days are in God's hand, not his own record."}
]},
{n:24, name:"The First Captivity", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 24:3",verse:"Surely at the commandment of the LORD came this upon Judah, to remove them out of his sight, for the sins of Manasseh, according to all that he did;"}, facts:["Did you know Zedekiah was not his birth name? Nebuchadnezzar renamed his uncle Mattaniah when he put him on Judah's throne (2 Kings 24:17).","Did you know the first deportation took ten thousand captives, including all the princes, mighty men, craftsmen, and smiths of Jerusalem (2 Kings 24:14)?","Did you know the LORD 'would not pardon' the innocent blood Manasseh shed, even after Josiah's great reforms (2 Kings 24:4)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Nebuchadnezzar make Jehoiakim in his days?", options:["His servant for three years","His captain of the guard","His cupbearer in Babylon","His tribute bearer for life"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:1",verse:"In his days Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up, and Jehoiakim became his servant three years: then he turned and rebelled against him.", insight:"Nebuchadnezzar came up, and Jehoiakim became his servant; pride that bows to no God ends up bowing to men."},
{q:"What did Jehoiakim do after three years of service?", options:["He turned and rebelled against him","He paid double tribute","He fled to Egypt","He made a covenant of peace"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:1",verse:"In his days Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up, and Jehoiakim became his servant three years: then he turned and rebelled against him.", insight:"Three years of service, then rebellion; vows made under pressure rarely survive comfort."},
{q:"Which bands did the LORD send against Judah?", options:["Bands of the Chaldees, Syrians, Moabites, and Ammonites","Bands of Egyptians and Ethiopians","Bands of Philistines and Edomites","Bands of Assyrians and Medes"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:2",verse:"And the LORD sent against him bands of the Chaldees, and bands of the Syrians, and bands of the Moabites, and bands of the children of Ammon, and sent them against Judah to destroy it, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake by his servants the prophets.", insight:"The LORD sent the bands; behind every invading army stood a sovereign God."},
{q:"Why did this come upon Judah?", options:["At the commandment of the LORD, for the sins of Manasseh","Because Jehoiakim was young","Because the priests had fled","Because the walls were weak"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:3",verse:"Surely at the commandment of the LORD came this upon Judah, to remove them out of his sight, for the sins of Manasseh, according to all that he did;", insight:"'At the commandment of the LORD came this upon Judah'; judgment was not an accident of politics but a sentence of God."},
{q:"What sin would the LORD not pardon?", options:["The innocent blood Manasseh shed, filling Jerusalem","The tribute withheld from Babylon","The broken covenant with Egypt","The neglected feasts of the law"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:4",verse:"And also for the innocent blood that he shed: for he filled Jerusalem with innocent blood; which the LORD would not pardon.", insight:"Innocent blood the LORD would not pardon; some sins write a debt that only judgment clears."},
{q:"What became of Jehoiakim?", options:["He slept with his fathers, and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his stead","He was carried captive to Babylon","He was slain by the Chaldees","He fled to Egypt and died there"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:6",verse:"So Jehoiakim slept with his fathers: and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his stead.", insight:"Jehoiakim slept with his fathers; death ended the reign that rebellion had already ruined."},
{q:"What had the king of Babylon taken from the king of Egypt?", options:["All that pertained to him, from the river of Egypt unto the river Euphrates","His crown and his throne","His horses and chariots","His sons as hostages"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:7",verse:"And the king of Egypt came not again any more out of his land: for the king of Babylon had taken from the river of Egypt unto the river Euphrates all that pertained to the king of Egypt.", insight:"Babylon took all from Egypt's river to the Euphrates; empires rise and fall at God's measurement."},
{q:"How old was Jehoiachin when he began to reign, and how long did he reign?", options:["Eighteen, and he reigned three months in Jerusalem","Eight, and he reigned thirty-one years","Twenty-one, and he reigned eleven years","Twenty-three, and he reigned three months"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:8",verse:"Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. And his mother’s name was Nehushta, the daughter of Elnathan of Jerusalem.", insight:"Eighteen years old, three months on the throne; some reigns are footnotes, and still answer to God."},
{q:"What was the name of Jehoiachin's mother?", options:["Nehushta, the daughter of Elnathan of Jerusalem","Hamutal, the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah","Zebudah, the daughter of Pedaiah of Rumah","Jedidah, the daughter of Adaiah of Boscath"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:8",verse:"Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. And his mother’s name was Nehushta, the daughter of Elnathan of Jerusalem.", insight:"Nehushta of Jerusalem; even a three-month king's mother is recorded."},
{q:"What did the servants of Nebuchadnezzar do at that time?", options:["They came up against Jerusalem, and the city was besieged","They burned the temple","They carried away the ark","They slew the priests"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:10",verse:"At that time the servants of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up against Jerusalem, and the city was besieged.", insight:"The city was besieged; no walls keep out the judgment God has decreed."},
{q:"Who went out to the king of Babylon?", options:["Jehoiachin, his mother, his servants, his princes, and his officers","The priests and the Levites alone","The captains of the army","The elders of the city"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:12",verse:"And Jehoiachin the king of Judah went out to the king of Babylon, he, and his mother, and his servants, and his princes, and his officers: and the king of Babylon took him in the eighth year of his reign.", insight:"Jehoiachin went out with mother, servants, princes; surrender was wiser than a siege God had ordained."},
{q:"What did Nebuchadnezzar cut in pieces?", options:["All the vessels of gold which Solomon had made in the temple","The brazen altar of the court","The pillars of the porch","The doors of the sanctuary"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:13",verse:"And he carried out thence all the treasures of the house of the LORD, and the treasures of the king’s house, and cut in pieces all the vessels of gold which Solomon king of Israel had made in the temple of the LORD, as the LORD had said.", insight:"The gold vessels Solomon made were cut in pieces; glory misused is eventually melted down."},
{q:"How many captives were carried away from Jerusalem?", options:["Ten thousand","Seven thousand","Three thousand","One thousand"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:14",verse:"And he carried away all Jerusalem, and all the princes, and all the mighty men of valour, even ten thousand captives, and all the craftsmen and smiths: none remained, save the poorest sort of the people of the land.", insight:"Ten thousand captives carried away; sin's bill comes due in full, not in part."},
{q:"Who remained in the land after the captivity?", options:["None remained, save the poorest sort of the people of the land","The priests and the Levites","The king's guard","The wealthy merchants"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:14",verse:"And he carried away all Jerusalem, and all the princes, and all the mighty men of valour, even ten thousand captives, and all the craftsmen and smiths: none remained, save the poorest sort of the people of the land.", insight:"Only the poorest remained; God leaves a remnant even in the ruin."},
{q:"How many men of might, and craftsmen and smiths, were taken?", options:["Seven thousand men of might, and a thousand craftsmen and smiths","Ten thousand of each","Five hundred of each","Three thousand in all"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:16",verse:"And all the men of might, even seven thousand, and craftsmen and smiths a thousand, all that were strong and apt for war, even them the king of Babylon brought captive to Babylon.", insight:"Seven thousand men of might, a thousand craftsmen; Babylon wanted Judah's strength, but God kept her story."},
{q:"Whom did the king of Babylon make king in Jehoiachin's stead?", options:["Mattaniah, his father's brother","A Chaldean prince","A priest of the temple","An officer of the guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:17",verse:"And the king of Babylon made Mattaniah his father’s brother king in his stead, and changed his name to Zedekiah.", insight:"Mattaniah, the king's uncle, set on the throne; God still ordered Judah's affairs through a foreign edict."},
{q:"What name did Nebuchadnezzar give to Mattaniah?", options:["Zedekiah","Jehoiakim","Jehoahaz","Shallum"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:17",verse:"And the king of Babylon made Mattaniah his father’s brother king in his stead, and changed his name to Zedekiah.", insight:"Renamed Zedekiah; new names from new masters cannot make new men."},
{q:"How old was Zedekiah when he began to reign, and how long did he reign?", options:["Twenty-one, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem","Eighteen, and he reigned three months","Twenty-five, and he reigned eleven years","Twenty-three, and he reigned three months"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:18",verse:"Zedekiah was twenty and one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Hamutal, the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.", insight:"Twenty-one, reigning eleven years; a long reign under a foreign yoke."},
{q:"What was the name of Zedekiah's mother?", options:["Hamutal, the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah","Nehushta, the daughter of Elnathan","Zebudah, the daughter of Pedaiah","Meshullemeth, the daughter of Haruz"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:18",verse:"Zedekiah was twenty and one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Hamutal, the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.", insight:"Hamutal of Libnah; her son would be Judah's last king."},
{q:"Why did Zedekiah rebel against the king of Babylon?", options:["Through the anger of the LORD, until He had cast them out from His presence","Because Egypt promised him aid","Because his princes forced him","Because Babylon demanded more tribute"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 24:20",verse:"For through the anger of the LORD it came to pass in Jerusalem and Judah, until he had cast them out from his presence, that Zedekiah rebelled against the king of Babylon.", insight:"Zedekiah rebelled 'through the anger of the LORD'; even rebellion serves the sentence God has spoken."}
]},
{n:25, name:"The Fall of Jerusalem", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 25:21",verse:"And the king of Babylon smote them, and slew them at Riblah in the land of Hamath. So Judah was carried away out of their land."}, facts:["Did you know Solomon's bronze pillars stood eighteen cubits tall, with three-cubit capitals ringed with pomegranates, before the Chaldeans broke them up for scrap (2 Kings 25:17)?","Did you know Zedekiah's last sight on earth was his sons being slain before him, and then his eyes were put out (2 Kings 25:7)?","Did you know the book of Kings ends with mercy? Evil-merodach lifted Jehoiachin out of prison, changed his garments, and gave him a daily allowance all his life (2 Kings 25:27-30)."], questions:[
{q:"When did Nebuchadnezzar's siege of Jerusalem begin?", options:["In the ninth year of Zedekiah's reign, in the tenth month, on the tenth day","In the eleventh year, in the fourth month","In the nineteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar","In the seventh month of the captivity"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:1",verse:"And it came to pass in the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, in the tenth day of the month, that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came, he, and all his host, against Jerusalem, and pitched against it; and they built forts against it round about.", insight:"Ninth year, tenth month, tenth day; God marks the dates of judgment as carefully as the dates of deliverance."},
{q:"How long was the city besieged?", options:["Unto the eleventh year of king Zedekiah","For forty days","For seven months","For three years"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:2",verse:"And the city was besieged unto the eleventh year of king Zedekiah.", insight:"Besieged until the eleventh year; judgment delayed is not judgment denied."},
{q:"What happened on the ninth day of the fourth month?", options:["The famine prevailed, and there was no bread for the people","The walls were broken","The temple was burned","The king surrendered"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:3",verse:"And on the ninth day of the fourth month the famine prevailed in the city, and there was no bread for the people of the land.", insight:"No bread for the people of the land; when God withholds, even the strong go hungry."},
{q:"How did the men of war flee the city?", options:["By night, by the gate between two walls, toward the plain","By day through the main gate","Through a tunnel under the wall","In ships down the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:4",verse:"And the city was broken up, and all the men of war fled by night by the way of the gate between two walls, which is by the king’s garden: (now the Chaldees were against the city round about:) and the king went the way toward the plain.", insight:"They fled by night toward the plain; flight is useless when God has appointed the pursuer."},
{q:"Where did the Chaldeans overtake Zedekiah?", options:["In the plains of Jericho","At the brook Kidron","In the wilderness of Sinai","At the gates of Riblah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:5",verse:"And the army of the Chaldees pursued after the king, and overtook him in the plains of Jericho: and all his army were scattered from him.", insight:"Overtaken in the plains of Jericho; you cannot outrun the sentence of God."},
{q:"What was done to the sons of Zedekiah?", options:["They were slain before his eyes","They were carried to Egypt","They were made eunuchs in Babylon","They were set free"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:7",verse:"And they slew the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes, and put out the eyes of Zedekiah, and bound him with fetters of brass, and carried him to Babylon.", insight:"His sons slain before his eyes; Zedekiah's last sight was the cost of his rebellion."},
{q:"What was done to Zedekiah himself?", options:["His eyes were put out, he was bound with fetters of brass, and carried to Babylon","He was crowned in Riblah","He was made governor of Judah","He was allowed to reign in Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:7",verse:"And they slew the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes, and put out the eyes of Zedekiah, and bound him with fetters of brass, and carried him to Babylon.", insight:"Eyes put out, bound in brass, carried to Babylon; the king who would not see God's word would see nothing more."},
{q:"Who came to Jerusalem in the nineteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar?", options:["Nebuzar-adan, captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Babylon","Nebuchadnezzar himself with his princes","Evil-merodach the crown prince","A captain of the Syrians"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:8",verse:"And in the fifth month, on the seventh day of the month, which is the nineteenth year of king Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, came Nebuzar-adan, captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Babylon, unto Jerusalem:", insight:"Nebuzar-adan, captain of the guard, came to Jerusalem; judgment's errands are carried out to the letter."},
{q:"What did he burn?", options:["The house of the LORD, the king's house, all the houses of Jerusalem, and every great man's house","Only the houses of the poor","The palaces of the princes alone","The storehouses of grain"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:9",verse:"And he burnt the house of the LORD, and the king’s house, and all the houses of Jerusalem, and every great man’s house burnt he with fire.", insight:"The house of the LORD burned with every great man's house; no building, however holy, survives a nation's apostasy."},
{q:"What did the Chaldean army do to the city?", options:["They brake down the walls of Jerusalem round about","They rebuilt the walls stronger","They left the walls untouched","They filled the gates with stones"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:10",verse:"And all the army of the Chaldees, that were with the captain of the guard, brake down the walls of Jerusalem round about.", insight:"The walls broken down round about; the city's pride lay flat in the dust."},
{q:"Who was left in the land, and to do what?", options:["The poor of the land, to be vinedressers and husbandmen","The priests, to keep the temple","The soldiers, to guard the gates","The scribes, to copy the law"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:12",verse:"But the captain of the guard left of the poor of the land to be vinedressers and husbandmen.", insight:"The poor left as vinedressers and husbandmen; God keeps a remnant to work the land the proud abandoned."},
{q:"What did the Chaldees break in pieces in the house of the LORD?", options:["The pillars of brass, the bases, and the brasen sea","The ark of the covenant","The golden altar","The tables of shewbread"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:13",verse:"And the pillars of brass that were in the house of the LORD, and the bases, and the brasen sea that was in the house of the LORD, did the Chaldees break in pieces, and carried the brass of them to Babylon.", insight:"The pillars, the bases, the brasen sea broken in pieces; even Solomon's bronze could not stand."},
{q:"Which brass vessels of ministry were taken away?", options:["The pots, shovels, snuffers, spoons, and all the vessels of brass","The trumpets and the harps","The crowns and the scepters","The chariots and the spears"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:14",verse:"And the pots, and the shovels, and the snuffers, and the spoons, and all the vessels of brass wherewith they ministered, took they away.", insight:"Pots, shovels, snuffers, spoons taken; the tools of ministry became the plunder of war."},
{q:"What is said of the brass of the two pillars, the sea, and the bases?", options:["The brass of all these vessels was without weight","It was weighed at a hundred talents","It was too little to carry","It was left in the ruins"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:16",verse:"The two pillars, one sea, and the bases which Solomon had made for the house of the LORD; the brass of all these vessels was without weight.", insight:"The brass was without weight; you cannot weigh what a nation lost in that day."},
{q:"How tall was one of the bronze pillars?", options:["Eighteen cubits, with a chapiter of three cubits","Ten cubits, with a chapiter of two","Twenty cubits, with no chapiter","Twelve cubits, with a golden top"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:17",verse:"The height of the one pillar was eighteen cubits, and the chapiter upon it was brass: and the height of the chapiter three cubits; and the wreathen work, and pomegranates upon the chapiter round about, all of brass: and like unto these had the second pillar with wreathen work.", insight:"Eighteen cubits of bronze, a three-cubit capital; the work of Solomon's best craftsmen ended as scrap."},
{q:"Whom did the captain of the guard take from the temple?", options:["Seraiah the chief priest, Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the door","Hilkiah and all the Levites","The singers and the porters","The king's wives"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:18",verse:"And the captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest, and Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the door:", insight:"Seraiah, Zephaniah, and the keepers of the door taken; judgment begins at the house of God."},
{q:"What happened to those brought to Riblah?", options:["The king of Babylon smote them and slew them at Riblah, and Judah was carried away","They were set free to return","They were made rulers in Babylon","They were sold as slaves"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:21",verse:"And the king of Babylon smote them, and slew them at Riblah in the land of Hamath. So Judah was carried away out of their land.", insight:"Smote and slain at Riblah; 'so Judah was carried away out of their land,' the sentence Manasseh's sins had written."},
{q:"Whom did Nebuchadnezzar make ruler over the remnant in Judah?", options:["Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan","Ishmael the son of Nethaniah","Johanan the son of Careah","An officer of the Chaldees"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:22",verse:"And as for the people that remained in the land of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had left, even over them he made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, ruler.", insight:"Gedaliah son of Ahikam made ruler; in the ruins God still appointed a governor."},
{q:"What did Gedaliah swear to the captains and their men?", options:["Fear not to be the servants of the Chaldees; dwell in the land, serve the king of Babylon, and it shall be well with you","Flee to Egypt before it is too late","Rise up and fight the Chaldees","Hide in the mountains"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:24",verse:"And Gedaliah sware to them, and to their men, and said unto them, Fear not to be the servants of the Chaldees: dwell in the land, and serve the king of Babylon; and it shall be well with you.", insight:"'Fear not... it shall be well with you'; God's counsel in captivity is quiet faithfulness, not frantic escape."},
{q:"In what year of captivity was Jehoiachin lifted out of prison?", options:["In the seven and thirtieth year of the captivity of Jehoiachin","In the eleventh year of Zedekiah","In the nineteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar","In the first year of Evil-merodach's reign"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 25:27",verse:"And it came to pass in the seven and thirtieth year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, on the seven and twentieth day of the month, that Evil-merodach king of Babylon in the year that he began to reign did lift up the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah out of prison;", insight:"In the thirty-seventh year, Jehoiachin was lifted out of prison; the book ends with mercy, and mercy is how God ends His stories."}
]}
]);
